)(1)(C)(i) safe-harbor percent (110% if > $150,000, or $75,000 MFS; else 100%). Absent → the engine assumes the high-income 110% (the larger-required, under-tax-safe direction). |\n| priorYearWasFull12MonthReturn boolean | §6654(d)(1)(C)(i): the prior-year safe harbor is available ONLY if the prior year was a filed 12-month return. Absent/false → the prior-year harbor does not apply and the required annual payment = 90%…§6654(d)(1)(C)(i): the prior-year safe harbor is available ONLY if the prior year was a filed 12-month return. Absent/false → the prior-year harbor does not apply and the required annual payment = 90% of current-year tax (the larger, under-tax-safe figure). |\n| priorYearCitizenOrResidentAllYear boolean | §6654(e)(2)(C): the prior-year-$0 penalty exception requires the taxpayer was a US CITIZEN or RESIDENT throughout the preceding year. A nonresident alien whose prior-year US tax was $0 because they…§6654(e)(2)(C): the prior-year-$0 penalty exception requires the taxpayer was a US CITIZEN or RESIDENT throughout the preceding year. A nonresident alien whose prior-year US tax was $0 because they were an NRA does NOT qualify; engine-invisible, so the (e)(2) exception is granted only when this is true (absent/false → not (e)(2)). |\n| estimatedTaxNextYear object | Opt-in, 2026 returns: next year's 1040-ES prior-year safe harbor (§6654(d)(1)(B)(ii), (C)). |\n| medicareTaxWithheld number | W-2 box 6 Medicare tax withheld, summed across W-2s. Used with medicareWages for the Additional Medicare withholding credit. |\n| taxableInterest number | Form 1040 line 2b: taxable interest (as figured on Schedule B line 4). |\n| ordinaryDividends number | Form 1040 line 3b: total ordinary dividends (as figured on Schedule B line 6), including the qualified subset. |\n| qualifiedDividends number | Form 1040 line 3a: qualified dividends (≤ ordinaryDividends) — taxed at preferential LTCG/QDIV rates |\n| reit199ADividends number | Qualified REIT dividends as Form 8995 defines them — §199A REIT dividends (≤ ordinaryDividends). 20% QBI deduction (REIT box-5 ONLY; PTP/business QBI out of scope, declines). |\n| netShortTermCapGain number | CONTAINER SCALAR - OMITTING THIS FIELD ASSERTS THE SCHEDULE DOES NOT EXIST ON THE RETURN; CONTAINER SCALAR - OMITTING THIS FIELD ASSERTS THE SCHEDULE DOES NOT EXIST ON THE RETURN; it does NOT mean $0. A schedule that exists and nets to zero MUST be sent explicitly as 0, because the section 6694 affirmation gates trigger on the schedule's EXISTENCE and omitting a zero-net schedule silently skips them. THE ENGINE CANNOT DETECT A VIOLATION - omission is indistinguishable from absence, so this obligation is enforced by the caller. Pre-netted scalar net short-term capital gain/loss (Schedule D). CONTRACT: this is the CURRENT-YEAR net, BEFORE any prior-year capital-loss carryover — NOT Schedule D line 15/16. \"Pre-netted\" means across LOTS (the alternative to capGainAggregates), never against a carryover; a carryover goes in priorYearCapLossCarryoverST/LT and is applied on top. Netting it in here as well applies it twice (an executed $12,120 under-tax). Lot-level/8949 detail and covered-basis decline on the scalar path (a broker-reported wash-sale disallowance computes via the capGainAggregates washSaleDisallowed path — see that field; it cannot be expressed as a pre-netted scalar); an affirmed §1256 aggregate is modeled via section1256NetGain (positive net, or no-election loss with the additional loss attestation; 40/60 split — see that field)."
